The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'isb-cgc-bq': {'reactome_versioned': ['pathway_hierarchy_v77', 'pe_to_pathway_v77', 'physical_entity_v77', 'pathway_v77'], 'targetome_versioned': ['target_synonyms_v1', 'sources_v1', 'interactions_v1', 'experiments_v1', 'drug_synonyms_v1']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage
• targetome_versioned.interactions_v1  
  – drugName / drugID: find all records that correspond to sorafenib  
  – targetID / targetName / target_uniprotID / targetSpecies: pick the Human (“Homo sapiens”) protein targets we want to evaluate  
  – expID + sourceID: allow a link to experimental data or publication evidence  

• targetome_versioned.drug_synonyms_v1  
  – synonym / drugID: discover additional spellings for sorafenib so every interaction row can be captured  

• targetome_versioned.experiments_v1  
  – expID: primary‑key to join with interactions_v1  
  – exp_assayValueMedian / exp_assayValueLow / exp_assayValueHigh / exp_assayUnits: apply potency filter (≤ 100, nM assumed)  
  – exp_assaySpecies: make sure evidence is relevant (usually Human) if needed  

• reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77  
  – uniprot_id: join with target_uniprotID to convert Targetome protein into a Reactome physical entity  
  – stable_id: Reactome PE identifier used in the mapping table  
  – name / location: optional description  

• reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77  
  – pe_stable_id: link to the physical entity  
  – pathway_stable_id: link to the pathway  
  – evidence_code: keep only records whose evidence_code = 'TAS'  

• reactome_versioned.pathway_v77  
  – stable_id: pathway primary‑key  
  – name / url: pathway description  
  – species: keep only “Homo sapiens”  
  – lowest_level: retain only rows in which lowest_level = TRUE (i.e. pathways that have no children)  

• reactome_versioned.pathway_hierarchy_v77  
  – parent_id / child_id: can be used to confirm “lowest‑level” status or build roll‑ups if necessary  

Typical filter/selection conditions we will need
1. LOWER(drugName) = 'sorafenib'  OR a match in drug_synonyms_v1  
2. interactions_v1.targetSpecies = 'Homo sapiens'  
3. exp_assayValueMedian ≤ 100 AND (exp_assayValueLow ≤ 100 OR exp_assayValueLow IS NULL)  
   AND (exp_assayValueHigh ≤ 100 OR exp_assayValueHigh IS NULL)  
4. pe_to_pathway_v77.evidence_code = 'TAS'  
5. pathway_v77.lowest_level = TRUE AND pathway_v77.species = 'Homo sapiens'  

Below are ten exploratory BigQuery SQL statements—progressing from very simple inspection to the core joins—that you can run (each limited to 20 rows) to understand the data needed to compute the chi‑squared results.

```sql
-- 1. Description:  Look at how sorafenib appears in the Targetome drug_synonyms list
SELECT DISTINCT `synonym`
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.drug_synonyms_v1`
WHERE  LOWER(`synonym`) LIKE '%sorafenib%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description:  Check what the canonical Targetome drugID for sorafenib is
SELECT DISTINCT `drugID`, `synonym`
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.drug_synonyms_v1`
WHERE  LOWER(`synonym`) = 'sorafenib'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description:  List raw interaction rows for sorafenib (all species, no assay filter yet)
SELECT DISTINCT `interactionID`, `drugID`, `drugName`, `targetID`, `targetName`,
       `target_uniprotID`, `targetSpecies`, `expID`
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1`
WHERE  LOWER(`drugName`) = 'sorafenib'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description:  Join interactions to experiments and keep only rows that satisfy the ≤100 nM potency rule
SELECT i.`interactionID`, i.`targetID`, i.`target_uniprotID`,
       e.`exp_assayValueLow`, e.`exp_assayValueMedian`, e.`exp_assayValueHigh`,
       e.`exp_assayUnits`
FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`   AS e
       ON i.`expID` = e.`expID`
WHERE  LOWER(i.`drugName`)        = 'sorafenib'
  AND  i.`targetSpecies`          = 'Homo sapiens'
  AND  e.`exp_assayUnits`         = 'nM'
  AND  e.`exp_assayValueMedian`  <= 100
  AND (e.`exp_assayValueLow`    <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueLow`  IS NULL)
  AND (e.`exp_assayValueHigh`   <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueHigh` IS NULL)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description:  Reduce to the unique Human sorafenib targets that pass the potency filter
WITH hp AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT i.`target_uniprotID`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`   AS e
         ON i.`expID` = e.`expID`
  WHERE  LOWER(i.`drugName`)        = 'sorafenib'
    AND  i.`targetSpecies`          = 'Homo sapiens'
    AND  e.`exp_assayUnits`         = 'nM'
    AND  e.`exp_assayValueMedian`  <= 100
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueLow`    <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueLow`  IS NULL)
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueHigh`   <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueHigh` IS NULL)
)
SELECT * FROM hp
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description:  Map those uniprot IDs to Reactome physical_entity stable IDs
WITH soraf_targets AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT i.`target_uniprotID`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1` AS i
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`   AS e
         ON i.`expID` = e.`expID`
  WHERE  LOWER(i.`drugName`)        = 'sorafenib'
    AND  i.`targetSpecies`          = 'Homo sapiens'
    AND  e.`exp_assayUnits`         = 'nM'
    AND  e.`exp_assayValueMedian`  <= 100
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueLow`    <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueLow`  IS NULL)
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueHigh`   <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueHigh` IS NULL)
)
SELECT DISTINCT p.`uniprot_id`, p.`stable_id`, p.`name`, p.`location`
FROM   soraf_targets            AS st
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
       ON st.`target_uniprotID` = p.`uniprot_id`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description:  For each mapped physical entity, pull TAS‑supported pathway memberships
WITH soraf_pe AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT p.`stable_id`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1`  AS i
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`    AS e
         ON i.`expID` = e.`expID`
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
         ON i.`target_uniprotID` = p.`uniprot_id`
  WHERE  LOWER(i.`drugName`)        = 'sorafenib'
    AND  i.`targetSpecies`          = 'Homo sapiens'
    AND  e.`exp_assayUnits`         = 'nM'
    AND  e.`exp_assayValueMedian`  <= 100
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueLow`    <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueLow`  IS NULL)
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueHigh`   <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueHigh` IS NULL)
)
SELECT DISTINCT ptp.`pathway_stable_id`, pt.`name`, ptp.`evidence_code`
FROM   soraf_pe                                             AS sp
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77`    AS ptp
       ON sp.`stable_id` = ptp.`pe_stable_id`
JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77`          AS pt
       ON ptp.`pathway_stable_id` = pt.`stable_id`
WHERE  ptp.`evidence_code` = 'TAS'
  AND  pt.`species` = 'Homo sapiens'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description:  1) keep only lowest-level Human pathways 2) count # of unique sorafenib targets per pathway
WITH soraf_pe AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT p.`stable_id`, i.`target_uniprotID`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1`  AS i
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`    AS e
         ON i.`expID` = e.`expID`
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
         ON i.`target_uniprotID` = p.`uniprot_id`
  WHERE  LOWER(i.`drugName`)        = 'sorafenib'
    AND  i.`targetSpecies`          = 'Homo sapiens'
    AND  e.`exp_assayUnits`         = 'nM'
    AND  e.`exp_assayValueMedian`  <= 100
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueLow`    <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueLow`  IS NULL)
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueHigh`   <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueHigh` IS NULL)
),
soraf_pathways AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT ptp.`pathway_stable_id`, sp.`target_uniprotID`
  FROM   soraf_pe                                            AS sp
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77`   AS ptp
         ON sp.`stable_id` = ptp.`pe_stable_id`
  WHERE  ptp.`evidence_code` = 'TAS'
)
SELECT  pw.`stable_id`, pw.`name`, COUNT(DISTINCT sp.`target_uniprotID`) AS sorafenib_target_ct
FROM    soraf_pathways                       AS sp
JOIN    `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77` AS pw
        ON sp.`pathway_stable_id` = pw.`stable_id`
WHERE   pw.`lowest_level` = TRUE
  AND   pw.`species`      = 'Homo sapiens'
GROUP BY pw.`stable_id`, pw.`name`
ORDER BY sorafenib_target_ct DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description:  Build the 2×2 contingency counts (targets vs non‑targets IN vs OUT of each pathway)
WITH all_human_pe AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT p.`stable_id`, p.`uniprot_id`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
  WHERE  p.`uniprot_id` IS NOT NULL
),
soraf_targets AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT p.`uniprot_id`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1`  AS i
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`    AS e
         ON i.`expID` = e.`expID`
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
         ON i.`target_uniprotID` = p.`uniprot_id`
  WHERE  LOWER(i.`drugName`)        = 'sorafenib'
    AND  i.`targetSpecies`          = 'Homo sapiens'
    AND  e.`exp_assayUnits`         = 'nM'
    AND  e.`exp_assayValueMedian`  <= 100
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueLow`    <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueLow`  IS NULL)
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueHigh`   <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueHigh` IS NULL)
),
pe_pathway AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT ptp.`pe_stable_id`, ptp.`pathway_stable_id`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77` ptp
  WHERE  ptp.`evidence_code` = 'TAS'
),
pathway_filter AS (
  SELECT `stable_id`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77`
  WHERE  `lowest_level` = TRUE
    AND  `species`      = 'Homo sapiens'
)
SELECT  pw.`stable_id` AS pathway_id,
        COUNTIF(st.`uniprot_id` IS NOT NULL)        AS in_pathway_targets,
        COUNTIF(st.`uniprot_id` IS NULL)            AS in_pathway_nontargets,
        COUNTIF(st.`uniprot_id` IS NOT NULL)=0      AS placeholder   -- just to view counts quickly
FROM    pathway_filter                 pw
JOIN    pe_pathway                     pp  ON pw.`stable_id` = pp.`pathway_stable_id`
JOIN    all_human_pe                   hp  ON pp.`pe_stable_id` = hp.`stable_id`
LEFT JOIN soraf_targets                st  ON hp.`uniprot_id`  = st.`uniprot_id`
GROUP BY pw.`stable_id`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description:  Compute chi‑squared statistic for every eligible pathway and pick the top three
WITH all_human_pe AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT p.`stable_id`, p.`uniprot_id`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` p
  WHERE  p.`uniprot_id` IS NOT NULL
),
soraf_targets AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT p.`uniprot_id`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.interactions_v1`  AS i
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.targetome_versioned.experiments_v1`    AS e
         ON i.`expID` = e.`expID`
  JOIN   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.physical_entity_v77` AS p
         ON i.`target_uniprotID` = p.`uniprot_id`
  WHERE  LOWER(i.`drugName`)        = 'sorafenib'
    AND  i.`targetSpecies`          = 'Homo sapiens'
    AND  e.`exp_assayUnits`         = 'nM'
    AND  e.`exp_assayValueMedian`  <= 100
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueLow`    <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueLow`  IS NULL)
    AND (e.`exp_assayValueHigh`   <= 100 OR e.`exp_assayValueHigh` IS NULL)
),
pe_pathway AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT `pe_stable_id`, `pathway_stable_id`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pe_to_pathway_v77`
  WHERE  `evidence_code` = 'TAS'
),
pathway_filter AS (
  SELECT `stable_id`, `name`
  FROM   `isb-cgc-bq.reactome_versioned.pathway_v77`
  WHERE  `lowest_level` = TRUE
    AND  `species`      = 'Homo sapiens'
),
in_out AS (
  SELECT pf.`stable_id`   AS pathway_id,
         pf.`name`,
         IF(st.`uniprot_id` IS NOT NULL, 1, 0) AS is_target
  FROM   pathway_filter pf
  JOIN   pe_pathway     pp  ON pf.`stable_id` = pp.`pathway_stable_id`
  JOIN   all_human_pe   hp  ON pp.`pe_stable_id` = hp.`stable_id`
  LEFT  JOIN soraf_targets st ON hp.`uniprot_id` = st.`uniprot_id`
)
SELECT pathway_id,
       name,
       SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 1 THEN 1 END)                       AS a,  -- targets IN pathway
       SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 0 THEN 1 END)                       AS b,  -- non‑targets IN pathway
       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM soraf_targets) - SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 1 THEN 1 END) AS c,  -- targets OUT
       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM all_human_pe) - 
       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM soraf_targets) - 
       SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 0 THEN 1 END)                       AS d,  -- non‑targets OUT
       -- Chi‑squared = n*(ad-bc)^2 / ((a+b)*(c+d)*(a+c)*(b+d))
       ( ( (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM all_human_pe) ) * POW( (SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 1 THEN 1 END) *
                                                         ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM all_human_pe) - 
                                                          (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM soraf_targets) -
                                                          SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 0 THEN 1 END)) -
                                                         (SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 0 THEN 1 END) *
                                                         ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM soraf_targets) -
                                                          SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 1 THEN 1 END)))
                                                       ), 2)
         ) /
       ( (SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 1 THEN 1 END) + SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 0 THEN 1 END)) *
         ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM soraf_targets) - SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 1 THEN 1 END) +
          ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM all_human_pe) - (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM soraf_targets) -
           SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 0 THEN 1 END)) ) *
         (SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 1 THEN 1 END) + ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM soraf_targets) -
          SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 1 THEN 1 END)) ) *
         (SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 0 THEN 1 END) + ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM all_human_pe) -
          (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM soraf_targets) - SUM(CASE WHEN is_target = 0 THEN 1 END)) )
       ) AS chi_sq
FROM   in_out
GROUP BY pathway_id, name
ORDER BY chi_sq DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

These ten progressively richer queries let you verify each data‑linking step, establish the potency‑filtered list of Human sorafenib targets, attach TAS‑backed Reactome pathway memberships, and finally compute (and rank) chi‑squared statistics so you can report the three most enriched lowest‑level pathways together with their target / non‑target counts.
